20269	JYe7gFBDDNw	42314	East Lynne	The beautiful Lady Isobel is left penniless when her father dies. She is offfered marriage by country town lawyer, Archibald Carlyle, who has recently purchased her father's estate of East Lynne. They have three children but Isobel becomes more and more jealous of Barbara Hare who has known Carlyle all her life and has frequent assignations with him as they are together trying to clear her brother's name, he having been wrongly convicted of the murder of a local man. When Isobel's erstwhile suitor, the aristocratic and shameless Sir Frederick Levison reappears, he plays on her suspicions and the two run away together. Isobel almost immediately regrets her decision and is deserted by Sir Frederick after she has become pregnant. Divorced by Carlyle, Isobel resolves to become a governess but is seriously disfigured in a train crash. Disguising herself, she applies to be a governess in the Carlyle household where she finds that Carlyle, believing Isobel to be dead, has married Barbara. The novel ends with several deaths.\n\nCategories: Melodramatic fiction	https://i.ytimg.com/vi/JYe7gFBDDNw/hqdefault.jpg	2025-11-26 18:05:52.764567+00	4114	\N
